<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32587" root="غو or غوى" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغَوَّاةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُغْوِيَّةٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>A
land in which one errs from the right way;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَضِلَّةٌ</span>; (K, TA; in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِضَلَّة</span>;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْوَاةٌ</span></b> ,
like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِهْوَاةٌ</span>; (K, TA; in the CK <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِغْواة</span>, like
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِهْواة</span>;) and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ مُغَوَّاةٌ</span>: (TA:) the pl. of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغَوَّاةٌ</span> is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُغَوَّيَاتٌ</span>; (K, TA;) and that of ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْوَاةٌ</span></b> 
is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغَاوٍ</span>. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  Also <i>Any well.</i> (AA, TA.)

